RETRO = '  <section id="humgeo-structural-repairs-20260917-20260918"><h2>HumGeo, September 17–18: the structural repairs before the QC climb</h2>\n    <p>Evidence window: the first paid remediation action on 2026-09-17 to hosted Course QC run 2 on 2026-09-18 (05:39Z, the job\'s own record). Course: the HumGeo v3 native TimeBack course. Every number and clock time below is copied from the section of the <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#humgeo-findings">HumGeo FINDINGS record</a> that the line links, on the course repository\'s main branch at commit ffcc7b61. This entry names mechanisms, not people. The QC climb that followed is the <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">September 17–20 entry</a>; the rules are on the <a href="lessons.html#humgeo-lessons-20260922">lessons page</a>.</p>\n    <h3>What landed</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li><b>598 native fails triaged by pool and class</b> with no ruling and no live change: 349 word-overlap shortcuts to the factory repair function, 122 not-taught findings to a per-item review, 81 quality, 38 checker errors, 8 real errors. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#triage-of-the-598-fails-2026-09-17-step-1-of-the-remediation-queue">Triage</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>280 served items replaced on 2026-09-17</b> through two sealed operators (152 choice-text repairs from the factory repair function, 128 judge-passed whole-item rewrites), each with capture 0 writes, execute with readback, replay 0 writes. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#served-item-replacements-executed-2026-09-17-steps-2-and-5">Served-item replacements</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>554 quiz rows repaired on 2026-09-18</b> so mastery gates, Train Your Eye and technique drills open; 537 topic-shape rows (one visible gate form per topic, 187 video relabels, 214 renumbers); 189 article text shadows so the hosted reader could see the instruction text. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#quiz-links-could-not-open-fixed-2026-09-18-session-incept-41-554-rows-repaired">Quiz links</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#topic-structure-had-five-separate-causes-ruled-2026-09-18">Topic structure</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#lane-a-article-text-shadow-executed-2026-09-18-0530z">Lane A</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Hosted run 2 read the course for the first time:</b> article_count 189 (run 1: 0), lesson_context_missing 0 (run 1: 5,017), severe pass rate 0.9077 (run 1: 0.0002). Its 442 question-quality findings were the first real content picture and became the redraft campaigns. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-2-2026-09-18-0539z-job_1359c54066f0417c886091b4daf972aa">Run 2</a>.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>What failed, why, and the correction that worked</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li><b>Quiz links would not open.</b> 350 of 438 quiz resources were written with the platform\'s own vendor id and no url; 204 gate rows also had an id without its prefix and a raw id for a title. Students saw a lesson error. Correction: a sealed repair set the fleet\'s working shape (QTI vendor, host, prefixed id, url, real title), found by comparing live rows with the 88 working rows and a sibling course. Rule: census every quiz resource against a working sibling before students see it. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#quiz-links-could-not-open-fixed-2026-09-18-session-incept-41-554-rows-repaired">Quiz links</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>One complaint, five causes.</b> A student-facing complaint about the topic structure traced to five separate mechanisms read from the live tree: unopenable quiz rows, three gate forms wired as three gates, videos typed as articles, duplicate sort positions from three numbering passes, and an approved removal of 901 video placements that looked like a bug. Correction: one sealed repair of 537 rows under the owner\'s ruling (one visible form, relabel, renumber instruction then practice then gate). <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#topic-structure-had-five-separate-causes-ruled-2026-09-18">Topic structure</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Hosted run 1 read no instruction text.</b> One check fired on 5,017 of 5,018 items because the reader extracts stimulus text without following an iframe, and the course served articles as iframe bodies. Correction: report the content result with that check set aside (99.84 percent clean), read the reader\'s code for the cause, add an article text shadow (189 writes) and file the reader gap with its blast radius. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-1-2026-09-17-1030z-step-3-job_49b854571fb045d583765d3868430998">Run 1</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>The render check returned no evidence.</b> 0 of 438 quiz rows mounted a render root; 146 rows had no screenshot because the walker parses only URL test ids. Correction: the run was ruled an instrument null, frozen, and render checks were ordered after the replacements; quizzes were later accepted as presentation-unverified with the owner walk as evidence. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#presentation-qc-run-ac714df3-2026-09-17-step-8-no-usable-render-evidence">Presentation QC run</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#2026-09-19-afk-run-owner-run-this-through-to-the-end">AFK run ruling</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>The practice fold hid practice from students.</b> Moving practice and gate rows onto the instruction lesson satisfied the ordering check but the player lists each resource as its own row, so every topic showed two Reading rows and no practice. Correction: undone the same day through the operator\'s undo mode (450 rows restored); the reader gap was filed instead. Rule: never reshape the live course for a QC instrument. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#phase-2-undone-2026-09-18-073xz-the-practice-fold-hid-the-practice-and-gate-rows-from-students">Phase 2 undone</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Videos read as Reading through two repair versions.</b> The platform merges resource metadata on PUT, so a candidate that dropped a key never read back; the player labels from activityType. Correction: version 3 added activityType Video and the Watch title; the owner confirmed on screen. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#videos-labelled-reading-and-duplicate-row-titles-fixed-2026-09-18-video-shape-repair-v1-to-v3">Video shape repair</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>22 judge verdicts lost mid-run.</b> An emit step rewrote records while the judge was open; the judge drops a verdict whose record changed between send and write. Correction: a backup of first-pass records and a byte-for-byte restore of unchanged judged records before any emit. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#factory-judge-over-the-rewrites-2026-09-17-steps-4-and-5">Factory judge over the rewrites</a>.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>What remains open</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li>82 video checks and 85 article checks live inside static documents and keep their pre-rewrite verdicts until an assets rebuild; recorded once as a ruled class. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#ruling-the-82-video-checks-are-deferred-recorded-so-they-are-not-re-raised-psych-pqc-qe-shape">Ruling</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#operator-2-population-2026-09-17-step-5-179-addressable-now-88-article-checks-routed-separately">Operator 2 population</a>.</li>\n      <li>The reader gap (stimulus text behind an iframe) and the render walker\'s id parsing sit with the QC service. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-1-2026-09-17-1030z-step-3-job_49b854571fb045d583765d3868430998">Run 1</a>.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>How the next course reuses this</h3>\n    <p>Read the hosted reader\'s code and run one small hosted job before the first structural write, so the first run scores content and not a blank read. Census every quiz and video resource against a working sibling course before students see it. Diagnose a complaint from the live tree and expect several causes. Pilot a lesson-shape change on one topic with the undo ready, and verify it on the rendered course, never on the QC score.</p>\n  </section>\n'

LESSONS = '  <section id="humgeo-lessons-20260922"><h2>September 17 to 20: what the HumGeo remediation record teaches the next course build</h2>\n    <p>Source: the HumGeo remediation record (<a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#humgeo-findings">FINDINGS</a>) on the course repository\'s main branch at commit ffcc7b61, read against this page, the <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">retro entries</a> and spec rules R8 and R9 on 2026-09-22. Of 60 rule-shaped statements in the record, 15 were already here in full. This entry carries the rest: 20 new rules and 25 amendments to rules already here in a general or partial form. Each names the Course Builder step it binds to and links the FINDINGS heading that holds the measured numbers.</p>\n    <h3>New rules</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n        <li id="humgeo-private-evidence-by-hash-20260922"><b>Cite private evidence by identity and hash; secure rubrics, answer keys, credentials and signed report URLs never enter the course record.</b> The HumGeo record names each native receipt by SHA256 and keeps the originals in the private root. <i>Builder step:</i> course record (FINDINGS) and evidence store. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#baseline-and-reporting-identity">Baseline and reporting identity</a> (H2).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-unique-and-occurrence-counts-20260922"><b>Report unique-item counts and occurrence counts separately; raw finding counts overlap within items and are never summed as repair counts.</b> HumGeo: 311 ordering, 767 question quality and 26 Faultless Bar findings sat on 598 items; run 2 counted 3,069 occurrences on 2,978 unique items. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (count reporting). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#baseline-and-reporting-identity">Baseline and reporting identity</a> (H3).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-no-blanket-exemption-20260922"><b>An instrument defect is ruled per finding class with item and check fingerprints, source evidence and a reviewer; it is never a blanket exemption.</b> HumGeo ruled 238 practice-without-instruction rows and 73 late-foundation rows by class with a row-by-row census, and left 4 prerequisite-drift rows as real. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (ruling record). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#first-queue-separate-item-defects-from-instrument-failures">First queue</a> (H5).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-four-review-decisions-20260922"><b>Every failed item gets one of four decisions (repair, drop candidate, retain-with-ruling, defer); a ruling clears zero QC points, a defer keeps the defect, and any changed input reopens the ruling.</b> The row records item id, finding ids, input fingerprint, EK/LO, placements, evidence, decision, reviewer and date, floor impact, the live action and the later hosted result. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (item decision ledger). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#item-decisions">Item decisions</a> (H8).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-course-own-floor-verifier-20260922"><b>Read the floor per pool from the course&#x27;s own blueprint and manifests, never from another course; land a floor verifier that censuses every lesson and gate form, counts a moved-and-dropped item once and goes red on a forced known-bad before the first drop.</b> HumGeo&#x27;s floors: at least one sync item per lesson, 15 per gate form with the thinnest form at 12 or more, fixed cumulative and final forms. <i>Builder step:</i> p3 bank gates / p6 drop gate (floor verifier). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#drop-floor-and-coverage-ledger">Drop floor and coverage ledger</a> (H11).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-render-check-scope-20260922"><b>A render check row whose page never mounted its root is not content evidence; uncaptured FRQs stay unmeasured; a render run never stands in for grading, result isolation or XP checks.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p7 walk and accept (render evidence scope). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-rounds-and-presentation-evidence">Hosted rounds and presentation evidence</a> (H16).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-capture-can-submit-20260922"><b>Bind test identity, the permitted capture and submission behavior and the secure-content boundary before launching a render capture, because the capture workflow can submit answers.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p7 render checks (launch preconditions). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-rounds-and-presentation-evidence">Hosted rounds and presentation evidence</a> (H17).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-scope-before-percentage-20260922"><b>Compare QC numbers only under the same check scope; another course&#x27;s percentage with checks disabled is not this course&#x27;s acceptance, and missing reviews, unresolved findings and local rulings are reported as separate facts.</b> Psych run 5 disabled the Faultless Bar and learning-science checks; HumGeo ran both on. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 bar statement. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#factory-precedent-and-acceptance-boundary">Factory precedent and acceptance boundary</a> (H18).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-filter-worklist-by-shape-20260922"><b>Filter a rewrite worklist by question type and pre-screen the live shape before any drafting spend; an MCQ redraft can never replace an extended-text item.</b> Campaign 3 wasted 88 drafts; operator 2 excluded 39 wrong-shape rewrites. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (worklist filter). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#campaign-3-and-hosted-course-qc-run-3-2026-09-18-owner-keep-working-until-everything-passes-qc">Campaign 3 and Operator 2 population</a> (H22).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-review-not-taught-first-20260922"><b>Review every not-taught finding against the topic&#x27;s teaching text with one quoted evidence sentence before redrafting; a taught item is a false reject and stays as served.</b> HumGeo: 59 of 122 were taught and kept; 63 went to the rewrite lane. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (review before rewrite). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#lane-c-taught--not-taught-review-2026-09-17-step-4-review-before-rewrite">Lane C taught / not-taught review</a> (H25).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-render-after-replacements-20260922"><b>A render run where no row mounted its root is an instrument null; freeze it and run render checks after the replacements land, never before.</b> Run ac714df3: 0 of 438 rows had a render root. <i>Builder step:</i> p7 render checks (ordering). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#presentation-qc-run-ac714df3-2026-09-17-step-8-no-usable-render-evidence">Presentation QC run ac714df3</a> (H26).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-record-deferred-class-once-20260922"><b>Record a deferred defect class once with its census, its route and the expectation that it keeps failing every run; change embedded checks by editing the authored source, rebuilding assets and republishing to the new key.</b> 82 video checks, 1.3 percent of judged items, deferred for the release. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (known-ruled classes). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#video-checks-82-d8-repairs-2026-09-17-step-6-not-standalone-items">Video checks and Ruling: the 82 video checks are deferred</a> (H28).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-measure-drafter-pass-rate-20260922"><b>Pilot each drafting model on a handful of items and pick by its measured structural pass rate before spending on the full run.</b> HumGeo measured 96 percent against 69 percent on the same worklist. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (drafter choice). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#factory-judge-over-the-rewrites-2026-09-17-steps-4-and-5">Factory judge over the rewrites</a> (H33).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-hosted-run-is-acceptance-20260922"><b>Treat the factory item judge as the gate and the hosted run as the acceptance; a judge pass can still fail the hosted reader, and the run&#x27;s cache-miss count shows which items it judged fresh.</b> One of 280 fresh replacements failed answer_in_stem after passing the item judge. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (acceptance versus gate). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-1-2026-09-17-1030z-step-3-job_49b854571fb045d583765d3868430998">Hosted Course QC run 1</a> (H37).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-signoff-gates-apart-20260922"><b>Report the Faultless Bar&#x27;s sign-off gates apart from its automated checks; a red sign-off gate is a pending signature, not a content failure.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p6 bar statement; p8 sign-off. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-2-2026-09-18-0539z-job_1359c54066f0417c886091b4daf972aa">Hosted Course QC runs 1 and 2 (Faultless Bar lines)</a> (H38).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-one-visible-gate-form-20260922"><b>Wire one visible mastery-gate form per topic; the blueprint&#x27;s extra forms are alternates for rotation, not extra gates.</b> HumGeo students saw three gates per topic until 136 form rows were tombstoned. <i>Builder step:</i> p5 tree (gate wiring). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#topic-structure-had-five-separate-causes-ruled-2026-09-18">Topic structure had five separate causes</a> (H41).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-no-sort-order-collisions-20260922"><b>Every renumbering pass checks for sort-order collisions with the passes before it; sub-lessons run instruction, practice, gate with no duplicate positions.</b> Three separate passes left duplicate positions in many topics. <i>Builder step:</i> p5 tree (renumber check). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#topic-structure-had-five-separate-causes-ruled-2026-09-18">Topic structure had five separate causes</a> (H42).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-rule-ordering-by-class-20260922"><b>Rule ordering findings by class (assessment-only lessons, title heuristics, real prerequisite drift), state the residue the ruling predicts, and confirm it on the next run.</b> HumGeo predicted 18 unit-level rows would remain; run 2 reported exactly those 18. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (ordering class rulings). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#ordering-check-rulings-hosted-course-qc-run-1-job_49b854571fb045d583765d3868430998">Ordering check rulings and Lane C1</a> (H45).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-shard-loop-inputs-20260922"><b>Shard redraft loop inputs so no command line carries the whole worklist; a hung loop is stopped and its items recorded as fails, not waited on.</b> One HumGeo loop hung 56 minutes on an oversized xargs line. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (input sharding). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#campaign-6-batch-6-and-hosted-course-qc-run-6-2026-09-19">Campaign 6 and run 6</a> (H52).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-owner-walk-is-render-evidence-20260922"><b>Where the render instrument cannot reach a resource kind, accept it as presentation-unverified by the instrument and record the owner&#x27;s walk as an enrolled student once as the evidence.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p7 walk and accept (presentation evidence). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#2026-09-19-afk-run-owner-run-this-through-to-the-end">2026-09-19 AFK run</a> (H53).</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Amendments to rules already on this page</h3>\n    <p>Each names the section that carries the general or partial form, then the part HumGeo adds.</p>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n        <li id="humgeo-fail-is-a-queue-20260922"><b>A hosted FAIL opens a queue row, not a verdict: keep the raw verdict, record the review decision and the live action in separate columns, and keep independent rows moving while one is blocked.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (split every failed item by route first). HumGeo adds: raw verdicts stay unchanged; a review decision and a completed live action are separate columns; blocked rows do not stop independent rows. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (queue record). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#first-queue-separate-item-defects-from-instrument-failures">First queue</a> (H4).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-bounded-retry-envelope-20260922"><b>A provider error or an oversized context is a missing verdict, not a fail: retry inside a bounded, supported envelope; never rerun the whole pool blind, swap the model automatically or truncate the teaching text.</b> Already here: <a href="retro.html#humgeo-native-publication-20260914">humgeo-native-publication-20260914</a> (36 provider errors named as their own class). HumGeo adds: the retry envelope: bounded and supported, no blind full rerun, no automatic model swap, no truncation of the teaching context. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (provider-error route). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#first-queue-separate-item-defects-from-instrument-failures">First queue</a> (H6).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-canary-control-then-sweep-20260922"><b>Prove a defect class with one canary and one unchanged control per rendering path, then sweep every member; a ruled false alarm leaves the raw score unchanged.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#design-assumption-article-coverage-20260912">design-assumption-article-coverage-20260912</a> (a passing subset must not close the whole population). HumGeo adds: one canary plus one unchanged control per rendering path before a sweep; the false-alarm ruling leaves raw scores as they are. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop and render checks. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#first-queue-separate-item-defects-from-instrument-failures">First queue (HG-QC-07) and Hosted rounds</a> (H7).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-triage-by-pool-and-class-20260922"><b>Triage every fail on two axes before ruling: its pool (which fixes the floor and whether a drop is even possible) and its class (which fixes the route); run the floor checker with the drops list before any drop lands.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (choice, extended-text and no-topic-code routes). HumGeo adds: the pool dimension with its floor (gates fixed per form, lesson checks keep at least one, rehearsal fixed); the per-class routes; the floor checker run before any drop. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (triage before rulings). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#triage-of-the-598-fails-2026-09-17-step-1-of-the-remediation-queue">Triage of the 598 fails</a> (H9).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-drop-suppress-not-delete-20260922"><b>A drop suppresses the item from publication and keeps its bank record, id and ordinal; every serving reference is rebuilt on both sides of a move and read back; deletion is a separate admitted operation, and unlinking never authorizes it.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#review-28-rounds">unanchored section &quot;Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync&quot;, item 4</a> (denylist and deleted-ID non-reuse). HumGeo adds: the three-step drop procedure; denominator reconciliation before a score claim; deletion as a separate admitted operation with fresh no-live-reference proof. <i>Builder step:</i> p5/p6 drop operator. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#drop-floor-and-coverage-ledger">Drop floor and coverage ledger</a> (H12).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-freeze-every-hosted-run-20260922"><b>Record the hosted job id the moment it exists and never invent one; freeze its configuration, input fingerprints, reports and email state in the run folder; define the changed set as payload, stimulus, placement pointer and judging context together.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921">apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921</a> (cache key, no cold flag); <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (commit the receipts you cite). HumGeo adds: record the job id the moment it exists and never invent one; freeze the run folder; the four-part definition of the changed set; stale reuse is not verification. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (run record). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-rounds-and-presentation-evidence">Hosted rounds and presentation evidence</a> (H13).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-explain-the-denominator-20260922"><b>Account for every run in four parts: denominator changes, repaired-item gains, provider errors and movement on untouched controls; explain any denominator change before comparing two runs.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (one run carries noise; a second run confirms). HumGeo adds: the four-way accounting per run; treatment versus untouched controls; a denominator drop explained before two runs are compared (run 2: 2,040 tombstoned occurrences, not missing content). HumGeo run 2 dropped from 5,109 to 3,069 occurrences because 136 gate-form rows were tombstoned on purpose. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (run comparison). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-rounds-and-presentation-evidence">Hosted rounds and presentation evidence</a> (H14).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-cold-run-is-a-receipt-20260922"><b>Quote every hosted number with its cache state; the cold run is a receipt for where the course stands, not a gate, and the cold population is measured and disclosed before any paid run.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921">apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921</a> (no cold flag). HumGeo adds: the owner ruling that the cold run is a receipt, not a gate; the warm-cache caveat on every quoted number; the cold population disclosed before spend. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (bar statement). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-1-2026-09-17-1030z-step-3-job_49b854571fb045d583765d3868430998">Hosted rounds and Hosted Course QC run 1</a> (H15).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-hold-only-the-dependent-action-20260922"><b>A missing shared capability holds only the action that depends on it; every other row keeps moving, and the course record never authorizes a platform change, a release or a timer.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-fallback-in-same-issue-20260921">apwh-fallback-in-same-issue-20260921</a> (file the fallback route in the same issue). HumGeo adds: a missing shared capability holds only its dependent action, every other row keeps moving; a findings ledger authorizes nothing outside the course. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (filing and holds). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#factory-precedent-and-acceptance-boundary">Factory precedent and acceptance boundary</a> (H19).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-verify-the-repair-output-20260922"><b>Verify every factory repair before it lands: clear of the original class, no new structural fail, stem unchanged; a repair that still echoes a stem word or adds an absolute term is rejected and joins the rewrite worklist.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921">apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921</a> (repair route with fatal codes). HumGeo adds: the verifier on the repair output and the reject route. HumGeo: 234 of 242 verified, 8 rejected. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (repair verifier). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#factory-d8-repair-run-2026-09-17-step-3-first-paid-action">Factory D8 repair run</a> (H20).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-census-where-text-lives-20260922"><b>Census where each item&#x27;s text lives before picking a replacement route (standalone item, video check in a static document, article check, writing slot); one operator reaches one shape.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-census-ids-before-embed-20260921">apwh-census-ids-before-embed-20260921</a> (census live ids before an operator embeds items). HumGeo adds: the shape classes and the rule that each shape needs its own route. HumGeo: 152 standalone, 82 video checks, 85 article checks and 39 writing slots each needed a different route. <i>Builder step:</i> item campaign (live-shape census). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#applying-the-234-d8-repairs-to-the-live-course-2026-09-17-step-3b">Applying the 234 D8 repairs, Video checks, Operator 2 population</a> (H21).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-teaching-text-in-prompt-20260922"><b>Compose every redraft with the campaign item rules, the lesson&#x27;s own teaching text and the QC findings; a rewrite that changes the stem routes through the judge and a full-item replacement, not the choice-text operator.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921">apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921</a> (fatal codes and target EK in the prompt). HumGeo adds: the teaching text in every prompt; route by what changed (choice text versus whole item). <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (prompt composer, route). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#rewrite-lane-through-the-enrichment-workflow-hermes-sol-2026-09-17">Rewrite lane</a> (H23).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-walker-id-resolution-20260922"><b>When a render or QC walker fails a whole kind of resource, read how it resolves ids and check the syllabus before calling it an outage; a walker that parses only URL test ids misses ids carried in the sourcedId.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-read-reader-first-20260921">apwh-read-reader-first-20260921</a> (read the reader&#x27;s code first). HumGeo adds: the id-parsing fact and the syllabus check that separates an instrument gap from an outage. <i>Builder step:</i> p7 render checks (id resolution). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#presentation-qc-run-ac714df3-2026-09-17-step-8-no-usable-render-evidence">Presentation QC run ac714df3</a> (H27).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-presentation-unverified-record-20260922"><b>Certify a repair by byte-level readback of the served XML; a row the render instrument never reached is recorded as presentation-unverified with a named decision for a person.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#native-terminal-receipts-20260914">native-terminal-receipts-20260914</a> (exact readback certifies the write). HumGeo adds: the presentation-unverified record and its decision for a person. <i>Builder step:</i> p7 walk and accept. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#video-checks-82-d8-repairs-2026-09-17-step-6-not-standalone-items">Video checks (82 D8 repairs)</a> (H29).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-no-emit-mid-judge-20260922"><b>Never rewrite judge records while a judge run is open; back up the judged records first and restore unchanged ones byte for byte, because the judge drops a verdict whose record changed between send and write.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#review-28-rounds">unanchored section &quot;Factory-canonical operating rules&quot;</a> (one writer owns each lane). HumGeo adds: the record-mutation guard: no emit during a judge run, a backup of judged records, byte-for-byte restore. HumGeo lost 22 verdicts this way in one run. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (record guard). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#factory-judge-over-the-rewrites-2026-09-17-steps-4-and-5">Factory judge over the rewrites</a> (H30).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-quote-the-ced-description-20260922"><b>Quote the target EK&#x27;s own CED description into every redraft prompt as a hard constraint; the EK code and the judge&#x27;s reasons alone left six items failing for five rounds.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921">apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921</a> (target EK named). HumGeo adds: the CED description quoted verbatim as a constraint, not just the EK code. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop (prompt). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#ruling-the-82-video-checks-are-deferred-recorded-so-they-are-not-re-raised-psych-pqc-qe-shape">Ruling on the video checks, redraft loop result</a> (H32).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-one-check-headline-20260922"><b>When one check fires on nearly every item, report the content result with that check set aside, read the reader&#x27;s code for the cause, prove the class on a fleet course with the same shape, then file it with the blast radius.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-read-reader-first-20260921">apwh-read-reader-first-20260921</a> (read the reader&#x27;s code); <a href="lessons.html#apwh-file-mismatch-day-one-20260921">apwh-file-mismatch-day-one-20260921</a> (file with a reproduction). HumGeo adds: report the content result with the one check set aside; prove the class on a fleet positive control before filing; name the blast radius. HumGeo run 1: 5,017 of 5,018 items carried lesson_context_missing; with it set aside 99.84 percent had no issue. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (headline reading). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-1-2026-09-17-1030z-step-3-job_49b854571fb045d583765d3868430998">Hosted Course QC run 1</a> (H36).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-quiz-resource-shape-20260922"><b>Census every quiz resource against a working sibling course&#x27;s shape (vendor, host, id prefix, url, title) before students see it; a row with no url or a bare id will not open.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-live-facts-become-rules-20260921">apwh-live-facts-become-rules-20260921</a> (a live platform fact becomes a rule). HumGeo adds: the quiz resource shape and the census against a working sibling course. HumGeo repaired 554 rows after owner screenshots showed quizzes that would not open. <i>Builder step:</i> p5 publish (quiz resource shape check). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#quiz-links-could-not-open-fixed-2026-09-18-session-incept-41-554-rows-repaired">Quiz links could not open</a> (H39).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-diagnose-from-the-live-tree-20260922"><b>Diagnose a student-facing complaint from the live course tree, expect more than one cause, and keep owner-approved removals recorded where the next diagnosis will read them.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-lesson-shape-two-readers-20260921">apwh-lesson-shape-two-readers-20260921</a> (verify on the rendered course). HumGeo adds: read the live tree, not the plans; expect several causes behind one complaint; record approved removals where diagnosis will look. Five causes sat behind one HumGeo complaint; 901 removed video placements were a ruling, not a bug. <i>Builder step:</i> p7 walk (complaint triage). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#topic-structure-had-five-separate-causes-ruled-2026-09-18">Topic structure had five separate causes</a> (H40).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-metadata-merges-on-put-20260922"><b>Expect the platform to merge resource metadata on PUT: a candidate that drops a key never reads back, the player labels a row from activityType, and an escaped ampersand in an iframe src breaks the page.</b> Already here: <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (video shape repair named). HumGeo adds: the four mechanisms behind the repair. Three operator versions were needed before rows read Video. <i>Builder step:</i> p5 publish (video resource shape). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#videos-labelled-reading-and-duplicate-row-titles-fixed-2026-09-18-video-shape-repair-v1-to-v3">Videos labelled Reading, video shape repair</a> (H48).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-correlation-not-cause-20260922"><b>When a rendering difference is explained by a field whose renderer rule was never read in bytes, record it as a correlation and leave the owner&#x27;s choice open; never write it as the cause.</b> Already here: <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (pilot then undo). HumGeo adds: the correlation-versus-cause label when the renderer&#x27;s rule is unread. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 lesson shape (pilot record). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#psych-quiz-card-pilot-2026-09-18-one-row-per-component-in-an-ap_one-course-pilot-undone">Psych quiz card pilot</a> (H49).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-refusal-is-a-readback-20260922"><b>Read an operator&#x27;s refusal as a readback of live state: a re-plan that refuses because the candidate is already live, or an enrollment that refuses because the learner already has the course, confirms the state without a write.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (commit the receipts you cite). HumGeo adds: an operator refusal read as a positive readback of live state. <i>Builder step:</i> p5 operators (refusal reading). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#2026-09-19-afk-run-owner-run-this-through-to-the-end">2026-09-19 AFK run</a> (H54).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-technique-checks-in-exam-form-20260922"><b>Write technique checks as exam-form questions with the technique taught in the explanation, because the judge reads a which-response-earns-the-point stem as a meta-question; page checks inside an article do not move the hosted score.</b> Already here: <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (FRQ Technique lessons rebuilt). HumGeo adds: page checks are outside the hosted score; the judge-design rule for technique checks. <i>Builder step:</i> article step (technique checks). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#2026-09-19-afk-run-owner-run-this-through-to-the-end">2026-09-19 AFK run</a> (H56).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-surgical-redraft-measured-20260922"><b>For a wording class on items that already pass, change only the flagged option and measure that stem, key and other options are byte-identical; a redraft that fails the judge leaves the served item as it stands.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#apwh-own-defect-classes-20260921">apwh-own-defect-classes-20260921</a> (a fixed-string class gets a free scanner). HumGeo adds: the surgical redraft with measured byte identity; the rule that a failed redraft of a passing item stays as served. <i>Builder step:</i> item campaign (surgical redraft). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#2026-09-20-owner-finish-the-course-e2e-tonight-these-distractor-items-are-the-last">2026-09-20 finish e2e</a> (H58).</li>\n        <li id="humgeo-passing-items-regress-20260922"><b>Treat a rewrite of passing items as a regression risk: it clears no old fails, so read each new fail as a real regression or reader variance before the next redraft.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (a second run confirms). HumGeo adds: the regression-risk rule for cosmetic rewrites of passing items. Run 11: 5 of 83 rewritten passes flipped, two of them real. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (regression read). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/humgeo-rebuild/blob/ffcc7b612251843502e4f0acfea2098103da6e14/FINDINGS.md#2026-09-20-owner-finish-the-course-e2e-tonight-these-distractor-items-are-the-last">2026-09-20 finish e2e</a> (H59).</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>Present already, no new entry: H1 (lessons.html#native-terminal-receipts-20260914); H10 (lessons.html, unanchored section &quot;Factory-canonical operating rules&quot;); H24 (lessons.html#apwh-never-freeze-factory-20260921); H31 (lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920); H34 (lessons.html#apwh-cap-at-factory-bounds-20260921); H35 (lessons.html#native-terminal-receipts-20260914); H43 (lessons.html#apwh-lesson-shape-two-readers-20260921); H44 (SPEC R9.65); H46 (lessons.html, unanchored section &quot;Factory-canonical operating rules&quot;); H47 (lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920); H50 (lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920); H51 (lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920); H55 (retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920); H57 (retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920); H60 (lessons.html#apwh-deterministic-fix-20260921). Full verdict table: the coverage file beside the course record\'s fold (coverage-humgeo.md). The September 17 to 18 structural repairs that precede the QC climb are on the <a href="retro.html#humgeo-structural-repairs-20260917-20260918">retro page</a>.</p>\n  </section>\n'

SPEC_ADD = "### R10. Rules learned on HumGeo not yet in R8 or R9 (2026-09-17 to 09-20)\n\n- R10.1 Cite private evidence by identity and hash; secure rubrics, answer keys, credentials and signed report URLs never enter the course record. (H2)\n- R10.2 Report unique-item counts and occurrence counts separately; raw finding counts overlap within items and are never summed as repair counts. (H3)\n- R10.3 An instrument defect is ruled per finding class with item and check fingerprints, source evidence and a reviewer; it is never a blanket exemption. (H5)\n- R10.4 Every failed item gets one of four decisions (repair, drop candidate, retain-with-ruling, defer); a ruling clears zero QC points, a defer keeps the defect, and any changed input reopens the ruling. (H8)\n- R10.5 Read the floor per pool from the course's own blueprint and manifests, never from another course; land a floor verifier that censuses every lesson and gate form, counts a moved-and-dropped item once and goes red on a forced known-bad before the first drop. (H11)\n- R10.6 A render check row whose page never mounted its root is not content evidence; uncaptured FRQs stay unmeasured; a render run never stands in for grading, result isolation or XP checks. (H16)\n- R10.7 Bind test identity, the permitted capture and submission behavior and the secure-content boundary before launching a render capture, because the capture workflow can submit answers. (H17)\n- R10.8 Compare QC numbers only under the same check scope; another course's percentage with checks disabled is not this course's acceptance, and missing reviews, unresolved findings and local rulings are reported as separate facts. (H18)\n- R10.9 Filter a rewrite worklist by question type and pre-screen the live shape before any drafting spend; an MCQ redraft can never replace an extended-text item. (H22)\n- R10.10 Review every not-taught finding against the topic's teaching text with one quoted evidence sentence before redrafting; a taught item is a false reject and stays as served. (H25)\n- R10.11 A render run where no row mounted its root is an instrument null; freeze it and run render checks after the replacements land, never before. (H26)\n- R10.12 Record a deferred defect class once with its census, its route and the expectation that it keeps failing every run; change embedded checks by editing the authored source, rebuilding assets and republishing to the new key. (H28)\n- R10.13 Pilot each drafting model on a handful of items and pick by its measured structural pass rate before spending on the full run. (H33)\n- R10.14 Treat the factory item judge as the gate and the hosted run as the acceptance; a judge pass can still fail the hosted reader, and the run's cache-miss count shows which items it judged fresh. (H37)\n- R10.15 Report the Faultless Bar's sign-off gates apart from its automated checks; a red sign-off gate is a pending signature, not a content failure. (H38)\n- R10.16 Wire one visible mastery-gate form per topic; the blueprint's extra forms are alternates for rotation, not extra gates. (H41)\n- R10.17 Every renumbering pass checks for sort-order collisions with the passes before it; sub-lessons run instruction, practice, gate with no duplicate positions. (H42)\n- R10.18 Rule ordering findings by class (assessment-only lessons, title heuristics, real prerequisite drift), state the residue the ruling predicts, and confirm it on the next run. (H45)\n- R10.19 Shard redraft loop inputs so no command line carries the whole worklist; a hung loop is stopped and its items recorded as fails, not waited on. (H52)\n- R10.20 Where the render instrument cannot reach a resource kind, accept it as presentation-unverified by the instrument and record the owner's walk as an enrolled student once as the evidence. (H53)\n- R10.21 A hosted FAIL opens a queue row, not a verdict: keep the raw verdict, record the review decision and the live action in separate columns, and keep independent rows moving while one is blocked. (H4; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R10.22 A provider error or an oversized context is a missing verdict, not a fail: retry inside a bounded, supported envelope; never rerun the whole pool blind, swap the model automatically or truncate the teaching text. (H6; amends retro.html#humgeo-native-publication-20260914)\n- R10.23 Prove a defect class with one canary and one unchanged control per rendering path, then sweep every member; a ruled false alarm leaves the raw score unchanged. (H7; amends lessons.html#design-assumption-article-coverage-20260912)\n- R10.24 Triage every fail on two axes before ruling: its pool (which fixes the floor and whether a drop is even possible) and its class (which fixes the route); run the floor checker with the drops list before any drop lands. (H9; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R10.25 A drop suppresses the item from publication and keeps its bank record, id and ordinal; every serving reference is rebuilt on both sides of a move and read back; deletion is a separate admitted operation, and unlinking never authorizes it. (H12; amends lessons.html#review-28-rounds)\n- R10.26 Record the hosted job id the moment it exists and never invent one; freeze its configuration, input fingerprints, reports and email state in the run folder; define the changed set as payload, stimulus, placement pointer and judging context together. (H13; amends lessons.html#apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921, lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R10.27 Account for every run in four parts: denominator changes, repaired-item gains, provider errors and movement on untouched controls; explain any denominator change before comparing two runs. (H14; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R10.28 Quote every hosted number with its cache state; the cold run is a receipt for where the course stands, not a gate, and the cold population is measured and disclosed before any paid run. (H15; amends lessons.html#apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921)\n- R10.29 A missing shared capability holds only the action that depends on it; every other row keeps moving, and the course record never authorizes a platform change, a release or a timer. (H19; amends lessons.html#apwh-fallback-in-same-issue-20260921)\n- R10.30 Verify every factory repair before it lands: clear of the original class, no new structural fail, stem unchanged; a repair that still echoes a stem word or adds an absolute term is rejected and joins the rewrite worklist. (H20; amends lessons.html#apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921)\n- R10.31 Census where each item's text lives before picking a replacement route (standalone item, video check in a static document, article check, writing slot); one operator reaches one shape. (H21; amends lessons.html#apwh-census-ids-before-embed-20260921)\n- R10.32 Compose every redraft with the campaign item rules, the lesson's own teaching text and the QC findings; a rewrite that changes the stem routes through the judge and a full-item replacement, not the choice-text operator. (H23; amends lessons.html#apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921)\n- R10.33 When a render or QC walker fails a whole kind of resource, read how it resolves ids and check the syllabus before calling it an outage; a walker that parses only URL test ids misses ids carried in the sourcedId. (H27; amends lessons.html#apwh-read-reader-first-20260921)\n- R10.34 Certify a repair by byte-level readback of the served XML; a row the render instrument never reached is recorded as presentation-unverified with a named decision for a person. (H29; amends lessons.html#native-terminal-receipts-20260914)\n- R10.35 Never rewrite judge records while a judge run is open; back up the judged records first and restore unchanged ones byte for byte, because the judge drops a verdict whose record changed between send and write. (H30; amends lessons.html#review-28-rounds)\n- R10.36 Quote the target EK's own CED description into every redraft prompt as a hard constraint; the EK code and the judge's reasons alone left six items failing for five rounds. (H32; amends lessons.html#apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921)\n- R10.37 When one check fires on nearly every item, report the content result with that check set aside, read the reader's code for the cause, prove the class on a fleet course with the same shape, then file it with the blast radius. (H36; amends lessons.html#apwh-read-reader-first-20260921, lessons.html#apwh-file-mismatch-day-one-20260921)\n- R10.38 Census every quiz resource against a working sibling course's shape (vendor, host, id prefix, url, title) before students see it; a row with no url or a bare id will not open. (H39; amends lessons.html#apwh-live-facts-become-rules-20260921)\n- R10.39 Diagnose a student-facing complaint from the live course tree, expect more than one cause, and keep owner-approved removals recorded where the next diagnosis will read them. (H40; amends lessons.html#apwh-lesson-shape-two-readers-20260921)\n- R10.40 Expect the platform to merge resource metadata on PUT: a candidate that drops a key never reads back, the player labels a row from activityType, and an escaped ampersand in an iframe src breaks the page. (H48; amends retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920)\n- R10.41 When a rendering difference is explained by a field whose renderer rule was never read in bytes, record it as a correlation and leave the owner's choice open; never write it as the cause. (H49; amends retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920)\n- R10.42 Read an operator's refusal as a readback of live state: a re-plan that refuses because the candidate is already live, or an enrollment that refuses because the learner already has the course, confirms the state without a write. (H54; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R10.43 Write technique checks as exam-form questions with the technique taught in the explanation, because the judge reads a which-response-earns-the-point stem as a meta-question; page checks inside an article do not move the hosted score. (H56; amends retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920)\n- R10.44 For a wording class on items that already pass, change only the flagged option and measure that stem, key and other options are byte-identical; a redraft that fails the judge leaves the served item as it stands. (H58; amends lessons.html#apwh-own-defect-classes-20260921)\n- R10.45 Treat a rewrite of passing items as a regression risk: it clears no old fails, so read each new fail as a real regression or reader variance before the next redraft. (H59; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n"

def patch(path: Path, anchor: str, block: str):
    s = path.read_text()
    assert s.count(anchor) == 1, (path, anchor[:60], s.count(anchor))
    path.write_text(s.replace(anchor, block + anchor))

